000300* ALTER, II-57. Syntax rule 1: the altered paragraph holds a
000400* single sentence that is a GO TO without DEPENDING, which is what
000500* lets the branch be compiled indirect -- a load from a cell and a
000600* register branch. ALTER stores a new address in that cell.
000700*
000800* This is also the statement that makes segmentation observable:
000900* an independent segment returning to its initial state means an
001000* altered GO TO reverting to the target it was written with.
